  "Each value describes one packet sent before the handshake, as a sequence of tags: <b 0x...> static bytes, <t> a 4-byte timestamp, <r N> random bytes, <rc N> random letters, <rd N> random digits (N up to 1000). Example: <b 0xd100000001><rc 8><t><r 50>. These are client-only parameters, they are never written into the server config; empty values are skipped, and an empty I1 turns the whole set off. Keep each packet under about 1472 bytes or it is fragmented on the way out, which is the signature this is meant to avoid. A config that grows past the QR code limit can still be downloaded as a file.": "Each value describes one packet sent before the handshake, as a sequence of tags: <b 0x...> static bytes, <t> a 4-byte timestamp, <r N> random bytes, <rc N> random letters, <rd N> random digits (N up to 1000). Example: <b 0xd100000001><rc 8><t><r 50>. These are client-only parameters, they are never written into the server config; empty values are skipped, and an empty I1 turns the whole set off. Keep each packet under about 1472 bytes or it is fragmented on the way out, which is the signature this is meant to avoid. A config that grows past the QR code limit can still be downloaded as a file.",
